# Orders → dashboards workflow (Large Cap)

When `Orders.csv` is updated or the user asks to refresh dashboards / “orders live”:

**Defaults for this large-cap book:** same-day trades only, start date **2026-08-19** (unless the user asks otherwise). Calendar title: **Large Cap P/L Calendar**.

1. **Enriched trades CSV** (repo root):
   ```bash
   python3 src/polygon/build_gains_from_orders.py \
     --orders_csv Orders.csv \
     --out_csv gainsandlosses_enriched.csv \
     --same-day-only \
     --from-date 2026-08-19
   ```
2. **Tradezilla JSON**: run `python3 src/polygon/build_trade_dashboard_data.py` with `--trades_csv gainsandlosses_enriched.csv` → `trade_dashboard_data.json` (uses `src/polygon/data/polygon` for SPY day direction when present).
3. **Serve**: `python3 scripts/serve_pnl_calendar.py` from repo root — `pnl_calendar.html` / `large_cap_pnl_calendar.html` (standalone with embedded CSV) and `tradezilla_dashboard.html`.

**Shortcuts (repo root):** `npm run orders:refresh` — rebuild only (already passes same-day + from-date); `npm run orders:live` — rebuild then `pnl:serve`.

Optional Polygon columns on the CSV (`enrich_option_day_highs.py`) are separate: API-heavy, not part of the default refresh script.
